To design a suitable iterative scheme, we divide the approximation solutions into local, and non-local parts, and introduce a localized corrector for balancing the non-compact support and non-divergence form parts of the new tensor error. For the local and non-local parts, we construct different perturbations to proceed with the iteration.

(1) For given $u_{q}^{\mathrm{loc}}$ with compact support, the local part of the approximate solution $u_{q}$ , we construct the perturbation $w_{q+1}^{\mathrm{loc}}$ with divergence-free and compact-support, based on the intermittent building blocks in [14, 46] such that $u_{q+1}^{\mathrm{loc}}=u_{\ell_{q}}^{\mathrm{loc}}+w_{q+1}^{\mathrm{loc}}$ . More precisely, $w_{q+1}^{\mathrm{loc}}$ is composed by four parts:

(a) The principle perturbation $w_{q+1}^{(\mathrm{p})}$ , which is constructed by using the box flows as in [46];

(b) The incompressibility corrector $w_{q+1}^{(\mathrm{c})}$ , which is introduced to correct principal perturbation $w_{q+1}^{(\mathrm{p})}$ to satisfy the incompressibility condition;

(c) The temporal corrector $w_{q+1}^{(t)}$ . We design it for cancelling the extra errors with the traveling-wave property. To ensure that $w_{q+1}^{(t)}$ has compact support, its construction is slightly different from that in [14, 46] and it is not divergence-free.

(d) The incompressibility corrector $w_{q+1}^{(\mathrm{tc})}$ . It is given to correct $w_{q+1}^{(\mathrm{t})}$ to enforce divergence free condition.
